# Import & export standards

Applies to application source (`**/*.{js,jsx,ts,tsx}`). Framework entry files (Next.js `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, etc.) follow routing rules first; align exports with those files when required.

---

## Exports

- Prefer **named (direct) exports** (`export const`, `export function`, `export type`, `export { x }`).
- Avoid `export default` except where a dependency or framework requires it (legacy APIs, routing).
- When a file has a single primary symbol, name the export to match the file (e.g. `UserCard` in `UserCard.tsx`).

---

## Imports

- Use **named imports with braces**: `import { thing } from './thing';`
- Do not rename on import unless there is a **naming collision** with another binding in the same file.
- **Order groups** (blank line between groups): (1) Node/built-ins, (2) external packages, (3) internal / relative modules.

---

## Exceptions

- **Next.js App Router**: `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`, `not-found.tsx`, `default.tsx`, and similar may use `default` exports when the framework expects them.
- **Third-party** patterns that require a default export may keep `export default` for that integration surface only.
